75 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 45 0 R
/E (Library management in most colleges is done manually using registers and paper records, which leads to errors, delays, and poor accessibility. Our project Library and Digital Resource Management System \(LDRMS\) aims to solve these problems by providing a complete web-based solution. The frontend is built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for a simple and user-friendly interface. The backend is developed using Node.js and Express.js to handle all server operations. MongoDB is used as the database to store book records, member details, issue and return history, and fine information. The system allows students to search and reserve books online, while librarians can manage book inventory, process issue and return, and calculate fines automatically. Email notifications are sent to students for due date reminders. The expected outcome is a fast, accurate, paperless, and fully digital library system that saves time and reduces manual effort for both students and library staff.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
76 0 obj
<<
