82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (The biggest problem is that all book records are maintained by hand, which causes mistakes and loss of important data. Students have to physically visit the library just to check whether a book is available or not, which wastes a lot of time. There is no online system to search, reserve, or access books from home.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
83 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (Fine calculation for overdue books is done manually by the librarian, which often leads to calculation errors and disputes. There is no automatic reminder system to alert students about their book return dates, so students frequently forget and get fined unnecessarily.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (Digital resources like e-books, journals, and research papers are not available on a single platform. Students have to search them separately on different websites which is very inconvenient.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
