/P 47 0 R
/E (Frontend is built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. HTML is used to create the structure of web pages. CSS is used to make the website look good and responsive on all devices. JavaScript handles all user interactions like form validation, dynamic content, and API calls.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Backend is developed using Node.js and Express.js. Node.js runs the server and Express.js handles all API requests. Separate APIs are created for user login, book management, issue and return, fine calculation, and notifications. All APIs follow REST architecture which makes communication between frontend and backend simple and clean.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Database used is MongoDB which stores all data in JSON-like format. Collections are created for Users, Books, Transactions, Fines, and Digital Resources. MongoDB Atlas is used for free cloud storage so no local database setup is needed.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
