159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (The Library and Digital Resource Management System \(LDRMS\) is a complete web-based solution designed to modernize and digitize the traditional library management process. This project directly solves the real problems faced by students and library staff in colleges where manual systems are still being used.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (Through this project we have successfully designed a system that automates all major library operations including book search, issue and return, fine calculation, digital resource access, and email notifications. The use of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for frontend makes the interface simple and easy to use for everyone. Node.js and Express.js provide a strong and reliable backend server. MongoDB Atlas ensures that all data is safely stored on cloud and accessible anytime from anywhere.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (This project is especially important because it combines both physical book management and digital resource access in one single platform which no simple existing system currently provides. The three tier architecture makes the system clean, organized, and easy to maintain and upgrade in future.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (As computer science students, this project gave us practical experience of full stack web development, database management, REST API design, cloud deployment, and real world problem solving. It helped us apply all the theoretical knowledge learned during our B.Tech program into a real and useful application.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (In conclusion, LDRMS is a practical, affordable, and beginner friendly solution that can be easily implemented in any college or institution to improve their library management system completely.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
